tellraw @a {"text": "Technology: The wheel, the potter's wheel and the spoked-wheel chariot", "color": "gold", "bold": true}
tellraw @a {"text": "Solid-wheel ox cart, spoked chariot with horses, and a potter's wheel.", "color": "white"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Mesopotamia, Eurasian steppe, Egypt, potter's wheel c. 3500 BCE; wheeled vehicles c. 3500-3300 BCE; spoked chariots c. 2000 BCE", "color": "yellow"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Solid disc wheels on carts appear almost simultaneously across Eurasia around 3500 BCE;", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "the light spoked-wheel chariot, from the steppe c. 2000 BCE, reached Egypt with the Hyksos", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "and became the Bronze Age weapons platform.", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "Early wheels were three-plank discs pinned together, turning on a fixed axle. Spokes,", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "bent-wood felloes and a rotating axle with lubricated hubs cut the weight to under 35 kg,", "color": "gray"}
tellraw @a {"text": "light enough for two horses to carry an archer at speed.", "color": "gray"}
